From: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas571x: retry the first register access after PVDD comes up

On the Yandex Station 1 the first write to the first TAS5751M (0x2a) after
the shared 20 V PVDD rail is switched on ends in an I2C bus error
("mv64xxx_i2c_fsm: Ctlr Error -- state: 0x2, status: 0x0") and the probe
fails with -EAGAIN; the second amplifier, probed once the rail is up, and a
re-bind of the first one both succeed. The rail takes longer than the 100 ms
settle time to come up. Retry the first access for up to half a second.

Signed-off-by: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c
@@ -1207,6 +1207,7 @@
  * the digital supplies may go. The bulk capacitance is board specific and
  * unknown here, so this is a generous guess.
  */
+#define TAS571X_FIRST_ACCESS_TRIES	10
 #define TAS571X_LATE_SUPPLY_OFF_MS	300
 
 /*
@@ -1335,7 +1336,18 @@
 		msleep(100);
 	}
 
-	ret = regmap_write(priv->regmap, TAS571X_OSC_TRIM_REG, 0);
+	/*
+	 * The first access right after PVDD comes up can hit the power stage
+	 * still ramping: on the Yandex Station the 20 V rail takes longer than
+	 * the 100 ms above, and the transfer ends in an I2C bus error (-EAGAIN
+	 * from i2c-mv64xxx). Retry it for up to half a second.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < TAS571X_FIRST_ACCESS_TRIES; i++) {
+		ret = regmap_write(priv->regmap, TAS571X_OSC_TRIM_REG, 0);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		msleep(50);
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		goto disable_late;
 
